The MIT license above covers the CODE in this repository.

Input datasets carry their own licenses and are NOT redistributed here; the
pipeline downloads them from their original sources. See docs/METHODOLOGY.md
for the per-dataset license table. Most are CC BY 4.0 (SoilGrids, Lembrechts
et al. soil temperature, ESA WorldCover, the Malaria Atlas Project friction
surface) or public domain as US Government works (USGS MRDS, USGS OFR
2004-1068). GLiM and the Maus et al. mining polygons are distributed via
PANGAEA under its standard terms. OpenStreetMap-derived quarry data is ODbL,
which carries share-alike obligations on derived databases.

tests/fixtures/pk2004_tables.txt is an extract of USGS Open-File Report
2004-1068, a US Government work in the public domain.
